{#- Case animation — the image block's 600 × 393 slot, holding a page that
    animates itself (Assets/embeds/...). The page is 620 × 406.1 and scales to
    whatever width it is given, so the iframe only has to hold that ratio.
    `loading="lazy"` keeps its ~1.7 MB off the first paint; the page starts
    playing once half of it is on screen, so nobody scrolls in mid-way. -#}
{#- A visual with its own box (`ratio`, e.g. "600 / 330") keeps that shape and
    a fixed 20px corner; without one it is the cover slot, as above. -#}
{#- `plain: true` drops the stroke and corner, so the visual reads as text content. -#}
<figure class="v4-case__animation{% if part.ratio %} v4-case__animation--free{% endif %}{% if part.plain %} v4-case__animation--plain{% endif %}">
{#- `viewport: true` sizes it to the screen instead of a ratio, leaving room for
    the section's title and text above it, so the whole thing fits in one view
    (the Challenquiz prototype, which scales its phone to whatever height it gets). -#}
  <iframe src="{{ part.src }}" title="{{ part.title }}" loading="lazy" scrolling="no"{% if part.viewport %} class="v4-case__animation-fit"{% elif part.ratio %} style="aspect-ratio: {{ part.ratio }}"{% endif %}></iframe>
</figure>
